S3a - REST v2.0 - FREEWARE - (c) by Marko Schuster 1994/96

This program needs GTLib v1.0 (not included, because REST is so small and
I distribute this program the same day as GTLib.ZIP)


Be sure you have installed GTLib.  GTLib was written by me, so I don't have
to write much about here ;-)


Rest shows the days, hours, minutes and seconds left to a event,
and how much % has gone already.

-----------------------------------------------------

You can have upto 11 entries.

Press the HELP-Button to get help about using the programm.

Press SPACE or PSION-E if you want to add/edit an event, move the cursor to
the event you like to edit/define and press RETURN (or DELETE if you
want to delete the event)

Type in the text for the event, the start-date&time and end-date&time and
press RETURN again.

If an event occures, an ALARM will be called, but only if REST is running,
otherwise this will happen the next time you start REST. The event is
deleted then.

Press ESC or Psion-X to exit.


The events will be saved to M:\opd\rest.dat


